```
D02 - Suspicious PowerShell Execution (T1059.001).
The two content analytics as Splunk searches. Copy ONE block at a time.
These are the frozen rules used across all four variants. The ``` ``` lines are Splunk inline comments.
Prerequisite: PowerShell script-block logging (EID 4104) enabled and the
Microsoft-Windows-PowerShell/Operational channel collected into index=endpoint.
```

```D02-A - process metadata (Sysmon EID 1). PowerShell by image OR original file name (survives a rename), with a download/execution indicator on the command line.```
index=endpoint source="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=1
(Image="*\\powershell.exe" OR OriginalFileName="PowerShell.EXE")
(CommandLine="*DownloadString*" OR CommandLine="*IEX*" OR CommandLine="*-enc*" OR CommandLine="*FromBase64String*")
| table _time host User ParentImage OriginalFileName Image CommandLine

```D02-B - script-block content (EID 4104). Any script block containing a download/execution indicator. Catches the decoded form of an -enc command; does NOT see through string-concatenation obfuscation. ProcessID is shown because 4104 has no ProcessGuid: it is the only way to tell the child's block from the launching PowerShell window's own block.```
index=endpoint source="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-PowerShell/Operational" EventCode=4104
(ScriptBlockText="*DownloadString*" OR ScriptBlockText="*Net.WebClient*" OR ScriptBlockText="*IEX*" OR ScriptBlockText="*Invoke-Expression*" OR ScriptBlockText="*FromBase64String*")
| table _time host ProcessID ScriptBlockId MessageNumber MessageTotal ScriptBlockText

```Telemetry-presence check used for variant 3 (proves an obfuscated run was logged even when the rules above return nothing). Searches fragments the rules do NOT key on.```
index=endpoint source="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-PowerShell/Operational" EventCode=4104 ("Net.We" OR "char]73" OR "192.168.10.250")
| table _time host ProcessID ScriptBlockId MessageNumber MessageTotal ScriptBlockText
